  "summary_md": "The Furnishings, Fixtures & Appliances group confronts a sluggish housing market and guarded consumer spending, yet this batch spans sharp extremes. Two self-help stories defy the macro: **LCUT** delivered a beat-and-raise on revitalized kitchen tools and surging Home Solutions, while **LOVE** is gaining share and building U.S. manufacturing to lock in margin gains. At the other end, **SNBR**’s Chapter 11 filing marks a total demand collapse, and **ATER** is liquidating entirely, leaving residual value tied to a speculative tariff-refund CVR. A cross-cutting theme is the pivot toward AI infrastructure among microcaps—**EFOI**, **MWYN**, and **XWIN** are touting data-center cooling or AI-platform narratives, though with limited validation. Capital-return moves (**HBB**’s dividend hike, **VIRC** insider buying) also compete for clicks in a week where tariff wildcards and housing softness remain the central backdrop.",
